window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-d902609b81a62396"]={"key":"ny_b1-d902609b81a62396","group":"ny_b1","uid":"d902609b81a62396","rank":78,"title":"dunmarrow ohio depot site selection memo","occupation":"real_estate_brokers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You’re Theo Ferreira, the broker advising Karin Boateng, VP supply chain at Dunmarrow Supply, and the real estate committee’s September session is the last practical opportunity to authorize an LOI for the company’s second Ohio distribution depot without putting the planned first-quarter opening at risk. The committee reviews occupancy recommendations monthly, but Karin wants this one resolved rather than carried forward as another ranked shortlist. The three finalists have all been toured and underwritten, and each is available on a ten-year term. The August underwriting assumed an initial requirement for ten loading positions and a month-18 requirement for thirteen; the operating team still stands behind that forecast. At 4180 Alloy Parkway, Meridian Commerce Center offers 34,800 sf, 32-foot clear height and eight existing docks. Its quoted effective rent moved from $9.84 per sf in August to $9.96 in September, and its model score moved from 88 to 87. The landlord will permit six additional docks, but the current proposal requires Dunmarrow to advance the $420,000 construction cost and provides for $300,000 of reimbursement after completion. The expansion election expires December 15, and the owner says the work can be completed by April 30. Dunmarrow’s current opening budget cannot absorb more than $300,000 of tenant cash before operations begin. The property is held in a single-purpose landlord entity formed for the acquisition; its ownership chart, evidence of signing authority, lender-consent position and financial support package have been requested but have not yet arrived, and no parent guaranty has been offered. The proposed possession date is January 15. At 2750 Flint Commerce Drive, Flint Logistics Hall offers 36,200 sf, 32-foot clear height and twelve existing docks. Its effective rent moved from $9.89 to $9.91 per sf, while its model score remained 88. The institutional owner has provided an ownership chart, audited financial statements and written confirmation that no lender consent is required for the proposed lease. Possession is proposed for February 1. The site has no contractual dock-expansion area or expansion option, and the tour team found no practical way to add a thirteenth dock without acquiring adjacent land that is not part of the offering. At 960 Canal Foundry Road, Canal Foundry offers 31,400 sf, 28-foot clear height and ten docks. Its effective rent moved from $9.62 to $10.18 per sf after the landlord withdrew part of the improvement allowance, and its score fell from 84 to 80. Possession is available January 1, but the building cannot be expanded within the offered parcel. The model awards twenty points each for effective rent and clearance; Alloy Parkway and Flint Commerce Drive both received nineteen rent points and eighteen clearance points in September, so those measures do not separate them. The model does not score landlord credit, funding reliability, enforceability of future dock rights or the operational consequences of missing the month-18 dock requirement. Karin views Flint’s delivered diligence and twelve day-one docks as the cleanest route to an on-time opening. The operating team views Alloy’s six-dock right as the only finalist-controlled way to support the approved month-18 forecast. Those requirements collide because Alloy begins below the initial ten-dock need, its construction structure exceeds the pre-opening cash limit, and the information needed to assess whether the landlord can fund its reimbursement may not arrive before the committee materials close at noon on September 12. The committee meets September 18, cannot defer the depot decision to October without jeopardizing the opening plan, and will not treat an LOI as permission to execute a lease or waive legal, title, environmental, zoning, physical-condition, insurance or authority diligence. Karin is willing to authorize pursuit of one site, including a conditional or time-limited approach if that is what your judgment supports, but she does not want two parallel LOIs, a recommendation framed as a tie, or a memo that postpones the choice to another study. Two defensible readings are open to you: the assignment can be treated primarily as protecting near-term opening certainty or primarily as preserving the approved month-18 operating capacity, provided the memo states which decision frame it adopts, weighs the cost of the other reading and commits to one address. If a critical item remains unavailable when the committee acts, the memo still needs to leave Karin with an executable path that distinguishes what the committee may authorize now from what must be verified before Dunmarrow becomes bound. Prepare a site selection decision memorandum addressed to Karin for the September committee session. Compare August with September, explain the material changes, identify the factors the model omits, make exactly one site recommendation and specify the LOI authority you want the committee to grant without implying that an LOI is a lease commitment. Use only the facts and figures in this brief; derived comparisons are welcome, but do not create market data, legal conclusions, construction estimates, environmental findings, incentives, travel times, probabilities or landlord financial facts. Keep the memorandum to no more than four pages, including any table or notes, and make it usable by an executive who has not participated in the tours. Write the finished document into the top level of the working directory using exactly the filename `dunmarrow_ohio_site_decision_memo.docx`.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `dunmarrow_ohio_site_decision_memo.docx` — Executive site-selection decision memorandum recommending one Ohio depot property and defining the requested LOI authority. (The document must be a readable DOCX no longer than four pages, compare August with September, make exactly one site recommendation, and use only supplied or transparently derived figures.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/dunmarrow_ohio_site_decision_memo.docx","bytes":41486,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/3fbf37b270df5d8316cf6d32ba831953eadd8c04c2fb943f204d9872b0f8aec4.docx","sha256":"3fbf37b270df5d8316cf6d32ba831953eadd8c04c2fb943f204d9872b0f8aec4","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"SITE SELECTION DECISION MEMORANDUM\nTO\nKarin Boateng, VP Supply Chain\nFROM\nTheo Ferreira, Broker\nDATE\nSeptember 12, 2026\nSUBJECT\nAuthorize one Ohio depot LOI for September 18 committee action\nDECISION REQUEST  Authorize me to pursue one non-binding LOI for 2750 Flint Commerce Drive, Flint Logistics Hall, on a ten-year term. The LOI should secure a defined negotiation period and preserve Dunmarrow's right to walk away. It is authority to negotiate only: it is not a lease, does not authorize lease execution, and does not waive legal, title, environmental, zoning, physical-condition, insurance, lender-consent or signing-authority diligence.\nRECOMMENDATION AND FRAME\nI recommend 2750 Flint Commerce Drive. The controlling frame is near-term opening certainty: Flint delivers twelve existing docks, the initial ten-dock requirement is met at possession without construction, and the institutional owner has delivered an ownership chart, audited financial statements and written confirmation that no lender consent is required. Proposed possession is February 1, later than Alloy's January 15, but materially more supportable on the evidence currently in hand. The cost of this frame is explicit: Flint has no contractual expansion area or option and remains one dock short of the month-18 forecast of thirteen. The operating team must own a plan for that residual shortfall; I am not treating an unoffered adjacent parcel as a real-estate solution.\nCOMMON COMPARISON | AUGUST TO SEPTEMBER\nProperty\nSize\n(sf)\nClear\n(ft)\nDocks\nexisting\nPossession\nEffective rent\nAug → Sep\nScore\nAug → Sep\nExpansion status\n4180 Alloy Parkway\nMeridian Commerce Center\n34,800\n32\n8\nJan 15\n$9.84 → $9.96\n(+ $0.12)\n88 → 87\nSix additional docks permitted; owner states completion by Apr 30.\n2750 Flint Commerce Drive\nFlint Logistics Hall\n36,200\n32\n12\nFeb 1\n$9.89 → $9.91\n(+ $0.02)\n88 → 88\nNo contractual expansion area or option; no practical 13th dock on offered parcel.\n960 Canal Foundry Road\nCanal Foundry\n31,400\n28\n10\nJan 1\n$9.62 → $10.18\n(+ $0.56)\n84 → 80\nParcel cannot expand; no controlled path beyond ten docks.\nWhat changed: Alloy rose $0.12 per sf and lost one score point; Flint moved only $0.02 per sf and held 88. Canal's $0.56 per sf increase followed withdrawal of part of its improvement allowance and its score fell four points. In September, Alloy and Flint are tied on the scored rent and clearance dimensions (19/20 rent; 18/20 clearance), so the model cannot decide between them. Canal's movement is the material rent change, not a peer movement.\nCAPACITY, TIMING AND COUNTERPARTY JUDGMENT\nCapacity is not interchangeable with a future right. At possession, Flint's twelve docks and Canal's ten meet the initial requirement of ten; Alloy's eight are short by two. At month 18, the requirement is thirteen: Flint is short one, Canal is short three, while Alloy would reach fourteen only if all six proposed docks are actually completed. Alloy's expansion election expires December 15 and the owner states completion by April 30, so it is not opening-day capacity and remains an unverified delivery commitment.\nAlloy also carries a funding and counterparty stack the score omits. The current proposal requires a $420,000 tenant advance and offers $300,000 reimbursement after completion, leaving $120,000 unreimbursed on the stated amounts and exceeding Dunmarrow's $300,000 pre-opening cash limit by $120,000. Reimbursement is exposure to a single-purpose landlord entity formed for the acquisition; no parent guaranty is offered. Its ownership chart, signing authority, lender-consent position and financial support package remain pending. Flint's delivered materials support present transaction certainty, but audited statements are evidence, not a guaranty or an unconditional obligation to fund work.\nModel omissions that matter here: landlord credit/funding reliability; enforceability and durability of a future dock right; and the operational consequence of missing the month-18 requirement. These are why the 87/88 scores do not substitute for broker judgment.\nREQUESTED LOI GUARDRAILS AND EXECUTABLE PATH\nIssue one site-specific, expressly non-binding LOI for 2750 Flint Commerce Drive, with a defined negotiation/exclusivity period so the recommendation remains usable while diligence proceeds. No parallel LOI or ranking exercise.\nState the February 1 possession target, ten-year term and business terms as subject to a mutually executed lease, committee reapproval and counsel review. The LOI must preserve withdrawal if agreed business terms or material diligence are not satisfied.\nRecord the known capacity condition: twelve existing docks meet opening need, but the property has no controlled path to a thirteenth dock. Assign the operating team to resolve the one-dock month-18 gap; do not represent adjacent land as available or committed.\nBefore lease execution, broker and legal must verify ownership and signing authority, title, environmental condition, zoning/permitted use, physical condition, insurance requirements and the written no-lender-consent position. Treat Flint's delivered ownership chart, audited statements and consent confirmation as received evidence subject to final verification, not as waivers.\nIf any critical item is still unavailable at the September 12 materials cutoff, the committee may still authorize the conditional LOI on these guardrails. Theo will obtain the missing item with the landlord; legal will confirm authority and diligence status. If unresolved by lease approval, Dunmarrow does not sign and the committee reconsiders the site; the September 18 authorization itself does not bind Dunmarrow.\nCOMMITTEE ACTION\nApprove the single requested action: authorize Theo Ferreira to issue and negotiate the conditional, non-binding LOI for 2750 Flint Commerce Drive under the guardrails above. This resolves the September decision while keeping lease execution, diligence satisfaction and final approval as separate later gates.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists at the top level under the exact filename dunmarrow_ohio_site_decision_memo.docx and opens successfully.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file and DOCX package integrity.","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact filename and location, then open or parse the DOCX without a repair warning."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete memorandum, including tables and notes, renders to no more than four pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX using a standard office renderer and count all pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The rendered document is executive-readable, with legible text, stable tables, sensible spacing and no clipped, overlapping or orphaned content.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered memorandum.","grader_hint":"Review the pages visually at normal reading size; minor stylistic preferences should not affect credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies Karin Boateng as its executive recipient and connects the decision to Dunmarrow Supply’s September real estate committee session.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Addressee, subject line or opening text.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent memo conventions if both the recipient and September committee context are clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum names exactly one recommended property by its full address.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation statement.","grader_hint":"The selected address must be either 4180 Alloy Parkway or 2750 Flint Commerce Drive to receive credit; Canal Foundry is not defensible on the supplied operating facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommendation is stated near the beginning in direct decision language rather than requiring the reader to infer it from the analysis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening portion of the memorandum.","grader_hint":"Look for an unambiguous recommend/authorize/proceed formulation in the opening executive section."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum deliberately adopts either near-term opening certainty or preservation of month-18 operating capacity as its controlling decision frame.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision rationale.","grader_hint":"Either frame is acceptable, but the author must explicitly choose rather than merely list both."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The selected property logically follows from the stated decision frame and the supplied facts.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation and supporting analysis.","grader_hint":"Flint naturally follows an opening-certainty frame; Alloy can follow a capacity-preservation frame only if the funding, timing and landlord-credit risks are confronted through credible conditions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum explains the material cost of choosing its decision frame over the competing reasonable frame.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Trade-off discussion.","grader_hint":"Expect a genuine concession: Flint sacrifices a controlled path to the thirteenth dock, while Alloy sacrifices near-term readiness and introduces funding and counterparty uncertainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum asks the committee to authorize pursuit of the selected site through an LOI.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision request.","grader_hint":"The requested action must be more concrete than general approval to continue evaluating sites."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum states that the LOI does not itself authorize lease execution or bind Dunmarrow to complete the lease.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authority limitation language.","grader_hint":"Accept standard non-binding, subject-to-lease or subject-to-final-approval language that clearly preserves the distinction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The property comparison uses a common basis across all three sites for size, effective rent, clear height, dock count, possession timing and expansion status.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparative table or prose.","grader_hint":"Verify that each named dimension can be compared across all three properties without searching unrelated sections."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Alloy Parkway is reported as 34,800 sf.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Property comparison.","grader_hint":"Allow formatting differences but no numeric variance; tolerance ±0 sf."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Flint Commerce Drive is reported as 36,200 sf.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Property comparison.","grader_hint":"Tolerance ±0 sf."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Canal Foundry Road is reported as 31,400 sf.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Property comparison.","grader_hint":"Tolerance ±0 sf."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly distinguishes the 32-foot clear height at Alloy and Flint from the 28-foot clear height at Canal.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Property comparison.","grader_hint":"Check both the values and their association with the correct properties."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly reports existing docks as eight at Alloy, twelve at Flint and ten at Canal.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Property comparison.","grader_hint":"Do not count proposed Alloy docks as existing docks."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum compares existing docks with the initial requirement of ten and identifies which properties meet that requirement at possession without construction.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Operational-capacity analysis.","grader_hint":"Flint and Canal have at least ten existing docks; Alloy has only eight."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum compares controllable dock capacity with the month-18 requirement of thirteen.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Operational-capacity analysis.","grader_hint":"Alloy can reach fourteen under the offered expansion right; Flint remains at twelve and Canal at ten on the offered parcels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies Flint’s one-dock shortfall against the month-18 forecast.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Flint analysis.","grader_hint":"The stated shortfall must equal 13 required minus 12 existing, tolerance ±0 docks."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies Alloy’s two-dock shortfall against the initial requirement before expansion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Alloy analysis.","grader_hint":"The stated shortfall must equal 10 required minus 8 existing, tolerance ±0 docks."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum recognizes that Alloy’s six proposed docks would produce fourteen total docks if completed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Alloy expansion analysis.","grader_hint":"Check the calculation 8 existing plus 6 additional equals 14, tolerance ±0 docks."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The possession dates are accurately associated with the properties: January 15 for Alloy, February 1 for Flint and January 1 for Canal.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing comparison.","grader_hint":"All three dates and property associations must be correct."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum notes that all three offerings contemplate ten-year terms.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or comparison text.","grader_hint":"Equivalent wording is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly distinguishes Alloy’s offered dock-expansion right from the absence of a controlled expansion path at Flint and Canal.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Expansion comparison.","grader_hint":"Do not award if speculative adjacent-land acquisition is presented as an available Flint option."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum compares August and September effective rent for each of the three properties.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period-over-period comparison.","grader_hint":"Both periods must be visible for all three properties, whether in prose or a table."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Alloy’s effective rent is shown as increasing from $9.84 to $9.96 per sf, a change of $0.12 per sf if the change is stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period-over-period comparison.","grader_hint":"Tolerance ±$0.01 per sf for any derived change."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Flint’s effective rent is shown as increasing from $9.89 to $9.91 per sf, a change of $0.02 per sf if the change is stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period-over-period comparison.","grader_hint":"Tolerance ±$0.01 per sf for any derived change."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Canal’s effective rent is shown as increasing from $9.62 to $10.18 per sf, a change of $0.56 per sf if the change is stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period-over-period comparison.","grader_hint":"Tolerance ±$0.01 per sf for any derived change."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies Canal’s rent increase as the material rent movement rather than treating all three changes as equivalent.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change commentary.","grader_hint":"Look for prioritization based on the magnitude of the supplied changes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum links Canal’s September rent change to withdrawal of part of its improvement allowance.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Canal change explanation.","grader_hint":"The causal description must not be replaced with an invented market explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The August-to-September model-score changes are correctly presented as 88 to 87 for Alloy, 88 to 88 for Flint and 84 to 80 for Canal.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Score comparison.","grader_hint":"Verify all six values and their property associations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum explains that the September model leaves Alloy and Flint effectively tied on the scored rent and clearance dimensions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Model interpretation.","grader_hint":"Equivalent language is acceptable if it accurately reflects their matching 19 rent points and 18 clearance points."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum accurately reports the shared September sub-scores of 19 out of 20 for effective rent and 18 out of 20 for clearance for Alloy and Flint.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Model discussion.","grader_hint":"Both sub-scores and both properties must be correctly represented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The period comparison explains what changed and why it matters to the current decision rather than merely reproducing two columns of figures.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Narrative accompanying the comparison.","grader_hint":"Expect decision relevance for the rent, allowance or score changes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies landlord credit or funding reliability as a factor omitted from the model.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Unscored-factor discussion.","grader_hint":"Accept counterparty strength, reimbursement collectability or equivalent professional terminology."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies enforceability or durability of future dock rights as a factor omitted from the model.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Unscored-factor discussion.","grader_hint":"A generic statement that expansion matters is insufficient unless the right itself is addressed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies the operational consequence of missing the month-18 dock requirement as an unscored factor.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Unscored-factor discussion.","grader_hint":"The document need not quantify an invented financial loss, but it must recognize an operational consequence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum does not treat the model score as a substitute for broker judgment where the model omits decision-critical risks.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall reasoning.","grader_hint":"Award when the conclusion is supported by explicit analysis outside the model."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum distinguishes current physical capacity from a future contractual right to create capacity.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dock and expansion analysis.","grader_hint":"Alloy’s proposed additional docks must not be described as existing or immediately usable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum recognizes Alloy’s December 15 expansion-election deadline.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Alloy timing analysis or proposed LOI terms.","grader_hint":"The exact date must be present."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum recognizes the stated April 30 target for completion of Alloy’s added docks.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Alloy timing analysis.","grader_hint":"The date should be characterized as the owner’s stated timing, not a verified guarantee."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum tests Alloy’s proposed expansion timing against both opening readiness and the month-18 requirement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Schedule analysis.","grader_hint":"Expect recognition that the proposed docks are not available at January possession but could address later capacity if delivered."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly states Alloy’s $420,000 tenant advance, $300,000 reimbursement and resulting $120,000 unreimbursed amount if calculated.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Expansion economics.","grader_hint":"For the derived difference, tolerance ±$1."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum compares Alloy’s required $420,000 pre-funding with Dunmarrow’s $300,000 pre-opening tenant-cash limit.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Capital constraint analysis.","grader_hint":"The collision between the proposal and the cash limit must be explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies a $120,000 amount by which Alloy’s required advance exceeds the pre-opening cash limit, if that difference is stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Capital constraint analysis.","grader_hint":"Tolerance ±$1."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"If Alloy is recommended, the memorandum does not accept the current expansion funding structure unchanged and instead makes conformity with Dunmarrow’s cash limit a substantive LOI condition.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation and requested LOI terms.","grader_hint":"Mark not applicable and award full credit if Flint is recommended; for Alloy, expect landlord funding, escrow, direct-pay, reduced advance or another credible structure without invented amounts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"If Flint is recommended, the memorandum openly accepts or mitigates the lack of a controlled thirteenth dock rather than implying Flint satisfies the month-18 forecast.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation and risk discussion.","grader_hint":"Mark not applicable and award full credit if Alloy is recommended; for Flint, expect an explicit residual capacity risk and an owner-assigned operational response that does not invent real estate rights."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies Alloy’s landlord as a single-purpose entity.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Landlord-risk discussion.","grader_hint":"Equivalent SPE or property-owning entity terminology is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum notes that no parent guaranty has been offered for Alloy.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Landlord-risk discussion.","grader_hint":"The absence must not be misstated as proof of insolvency or default risk."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum treats Alloy’s reimbursement as counterparty exposure requiring protection rather than as equivalent to an immediate reduction in Dunmarrow’s cash outlay.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Expansion economics and landlord-credit discussion.","grader_hint":"Look for timing, collectability, security or funding-risk analysis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly identifies the four pending Alloy diligence categories: ownership chart, signing authority, lender-consent position and financial support package.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pending-items discussion.","grader_hint":"All four must be present; grouping them in concise prose is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum contrasts Alloy’s missing counterparty package with Flint’s delivered ownership chart, audited financial statements and no-lender-consent confirmation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Landlord comparison.","grader_hint":"The comparison should explain why Flint offers greater present transaction certainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum distinguishes evidence that has been delivered from facts or protections that remain unverified.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Diligence and recommendation language.","grader_hint":"Look for disciplined use of supplied, pending, subject to verification or equivalent status language."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The landlord-credit analysis avoids equating audited financial statements with a guaranty or an unconditional obligation to fund tenant work.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Flint and Alloy counterparty analysis.","grader_hint":"Award when the document uses the delivered Flint evidence appropriately without overstating its legal effect."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposed LOI authority includes business terms that directly address the material risk of the selected site.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Requested authorization or LOI guardrails.","grader_hint":"For Alloy, expect expansion, funding, reimbursement security and delivery protections; for Flint, expect possession certainty and acknowledgment or management of the dock-capacity limitation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R57","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Any proposed expansion right is described as requiring documentation in the lease or other binding property agreement rather than relying on an informal statement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"LOI or lease-condition discussion.","grader_hint":"Accept language calling for a defined right, exhibit, premises control, construction obligation or comparable enforceable documentation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R58","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"If Alloy is selected, the memorandum calls for objective definition of dock scope, responsibility, timing and remedy for non-delivery.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Alloy LOI conditions.","grader_hint":"Mark not applicable and award full credit if Flint is selected. The submission need not draft clauses, but it must identify these core protections."},{"rubric_item_id":"R59","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum addresses how any landlord reimbursement would be secured or made independent of unsupported future landlord liquidity.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Funding protection.","grader_hint":"Accept escrow, letter of credit, direct landlord payment, verified committed funds, offset rights subject to documentation or another credible protection; do not require a specific mechanism."},{"rubric_item_id":"R60","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum seeks enough site control or negotiating protection to prevent the recommendation from becoming unusable while lease diligence proceeds.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"LOI terms or execution path.","grader_hint":"Look for exclusivity, a defined negotiation period, withdrawal rights or equivalent practical protection without requiring invented dates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R61","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum preserves Dunmarrow’s ability to exit if material diligence, authority or agreed business conditions are not satisfied.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conditions and fallback path.","grader_hint":"The exit right may be expressed through non-binding LOI status, conditions precedent or committee reapproval before lease execution."},{"rubric_item_id":"R62","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum preserves legal review before lease execution.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Diligence conditions.","grader_hint":"Equivalent counsel review or final legal approval language is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R63","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum preserves verification of ownership and signing authority before Dunmarrow becomes bound.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Diligence conditions.","grader_hint":"Both ownership and authority should be covered explicitly or by unmistakable equivalent language."},{"rubric_item_id":"R64","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum preserves confirmation of any required lender consent before lease execution.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Diligence conditions.","grader_hint":"Credit is appropriate even if the selected site is Flint, provided the supplied no-consent confirmation is acknowledged and subject to final verification."},{"rubric_item_id":"R65","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum preserves appropriate property diligence covering title, environmental condition, zoning or permitted use, and physical condition without asserting outcomes not supplied.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Diligence scope.","grader_hint":"All four areas must be preserved as checks or conditions; the document must not claim that they have passed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R66","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum preserves insurance review and any other final lease-approval controls without turning the memo into a legal opinion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Diligence and authority language.","grader_hint":"Look for appropriate referral to legal, risk or authorized reviewers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R67","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum supplies an executable path if a critical pending item is still unavailable when the committee acts.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contingency or conditional-authorization language.","grader_hint":"A satisfactory path identifies what can be authorized now, what remains conditional and what happens if the condition is not met; it must not simply say to wait."},{"rubric_item_id":"R68","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The failure path assigns a clear owner for resolving or verifying each critical condition.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action ownership.","grader_hint":"Accept role-based ownership such as broker, legal counsel, supply-chain lead or landlord; invented personal names are unnecessary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R69","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The failure path contains a decision point or timing trigger tied to the committee, LOI or lease process.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contingency timing.","grader_hint":"Accept the September 12 materials cutoff, September 18 meeting, an LOI expiry, a diligence deadline or another non-invented process trigger."},{"rubric_item_id":"R70","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum distinguishes authorization to negotiate or issue an LOI from authorization to sign a lease and from satisfaction of diligence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Governance and authority language.","grader_hint":"All three stages should remain conceptually separate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R71","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The conclusion restates the single requested committee decision and does not dissolve into a further ranking exercise or an open-ended request for more study.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closing section.","grader_hint":"The final substantive message should leave Karin knowing what to approve."},{"rubric_item_id":"R72","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum can be acted upon by an executive who did not attend the tours without asking the author to identify the selected site, principal trade-off, authority requested or unresolved conditions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire memorandum.","grader_hint":"Review for practical self-containment, not merely factual completeness."},{"rubric_item_id":"R73","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Facts, figures, property names, recommendation, LOI conditions and conclusion remain internally consistent throughout the memorandum.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire memorandum.","grader_hint":"Check especially that figures in a comparison table agree with the narrative and that conditions apply to the site actually selected."},{"rubric_item_id":"R74","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The writing is concise, commercially professional and proportionate to an executive decision memorandum.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire memorandum.","grader_hint":"Award based on clarity, prioritization and decision usefulness rather than decorative formatting."},{"rubric_item_id":"P01","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum recommends multiple sites, issues a ranked shortlist, proposes parallel LOIs or otherwise fails to commit to one address.","weight":-8.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation, alternatives and conclusion.","grader_hint":"Apply once if the document advances more than one property for authorization or makes the choice contingent on a later comparative study."},{"rubric_item_id":"P02","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum invents unsupported market data, legal conclusions, construction estimates, environmental findings, incentives, travel times, probabilities, financial facts or other decision figures.","weight":-7.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire memorandum.","grader_hint":"Do not penalize transparent arithmetic derived solely from supplied numbers. Apply when unsupported information is presented as fact or used to justify the recommendation."},{"rubric_item_id":"P03","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum presents the LOI or committee action as a binding lease commitment, a waiver of diligence or authority to execute the lease.","weight":-8.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authority request, conditions and conclusion.","grader_hint":"Apply when the document affirmatively overstates authority, not merely when its limiting language is weak."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Dunmarrow Supply’s real estate committee needs its broker’s written recommendation before authorizing pursuit of one of three Ohio distribution properties. The decision must reconcile opening certainty, future dock capacity, landlord-credit risk and the limits of an LOI.","difficulty_sources":["Two leading sites are tied on the model dimensions, requiring judgment about unpriced landlord-credit and expansion-right risks.","Near-term opening certainty conflicts with the approved month-18 dock-capacity requirement.","The committee deadline may arrive before critical landlord diligence, requiring a bounded failure path rather than deferral.","The memorandum must compare periods, derive material changes and convert the recommendation into executable but non-binding LOI authority."],"authoring_plan":{"solver_instance":"A commercial real estate broker prepares an executive memorandum for Dunmarrow Supply’s September committee meeting using only the facts embedded in the request.","behavior_specification":["Produce one readable DOCX under the exact required filename.","Select exactly one address and identify the controlling decision frame.","Compare the August and September underwriting on a common basis.","Treat model scores as incomplete because they omit counterparty quality, expansion-right enforceability and operating consequences.","Translate the recommendation into bounded LOI authority rather than lease authority.","Provide a conditional execution path for any unresolved critical diligence."],"imperfections_and_tensions":["Alloy and Flint are tied on September effective-rent and clearance sub-scores, so the scoring model cannot determine the result.","Alloy is below the initial dock requirement but has the only controlled route to exceed the month-18 requirement.","Flint meets the initial dock requirement and offers stronger delivered landlord diligence but is one dock short at month 18 with no controlled expansion route.","Alloy’s required $420,000 advance exceeds Dunmarrow’s $300,000 pre-opening cash limit by $120,000.","Alloy’s promised $300,000 reimbursement is exposed to an unverified single-purpose landlord with no offered parent guaranty.","The committee cannot defer, while critical Alloy ownership, authority, consent and financial-support information may remain unavailable at the materials cutoff.","The committee may authorize an LOI but may not authorize lease execution or waive diligence."],"gold_relationships":["Initial dock gap equals initial requirement of 10 minus existing docks: Alloy is short 2; Flint and Canal are not short initially.","Month-18 dock gap equals requirement of 13 minus controlled dock capacity: Flint is short 1 and Canal is short 3; Alloy reaches 14 only if all six offered docks are completed.","Alloy’s tenant-funded expansion amount exceeds the pre-opening cash limit by $120,000.","Alloy’s proposed unreimbursed construction amount is $120,000, but reimbursement timing and collectability remain separate risks.","Period rent changes are Alloy +$0.12 per sf, Flint +$0.02 per sf and Canal +$0.56 per sf.","Model-score changes are Alloy -1, Flint 0 and Canal -4.","A Flint recommendation is defensible only when near-term opening certainty controls and the month-18 capacity shortfall is explicitly accepted or operationally managed.","An Alloy recommendation is defensible only when month-18 capacity controls and the LOI conditions cure or contain the initial dock gap, cash-limit conflict, reimbursement exposure and missing landlord diligence.","Canal is not a defensible recommendation because its area falls below the stated 30,000–38,000 shortlist context only narrowly? No: its 31,400 sf remains within the range, but its lower clearance, inability to expand, month-18 dock deficit, withdrawn allowance and deteriorating score make it inferior on the supplied facts. The gold must rely on these actual disadvantages and must not claim Canal is outside the size range.","An acceptable LOI path is non-binding, site-specific, conditioned on final documentation and diligence, and separate from lease execution authority."],"acceptable_verdicts":[{"selected_site":"2750 Flint Commerce Drive","decision_frame":"Near-term opening certainty","required_concessions":"Acknowledge that twelve docks do not satisfy the month-18 forecast of thirteen and that no controlled expansion right exists.","required_execution_logic":"Authorize one non-binding LOI while preserving normal lease diligence and assigning an operational owner to address the forecasted one-dock capacity gap."},{"selected_site":"4180 Alloy Parkway","decision_frame":"Preservation of month-18 operating capacity","required_concessions":"Acknowledge that eight existing docks miss the initial requirement, the advance exceeds the cash limit, reimbursement is exposed to unverified landlord credit, and key authority and consent evidence is pending.","required_execution_logic":"Authorize only a conditional, non-binding LOI that secures enforceable expansion scope and timing, restructures or secures funding within the cash limit, protects reimbursement, and permits withdrawal if critical landlord or property diligence fails."}],"unacceptable_verdict":"960 Canal Foundry Road should not be selected because the supplied record shows lower clearance, no expansion path, a three-dock month-18 deficit, the largest rent deterioration and a four-point score decline without an offsetting unpriced advantage.","must_not_assert":["That Alloy’s landlord is insolvent, unable to reimburse Dunmarrow or legally unauthorized to lease the property.","That Flint’s audited financial statements constitute a guaranty or establish an unconditional construction-funding obligation.","That any site has passed title, zoning, environmental, physical-condition, insurance or legal review.","That adjacent land is available to Flint.","That the April 30 Alloy construction statement is a guaranteed completion date.","That committee authorization of an LOI authorizes execution of a lease.","Any market rent, incentive, travel-time, construction-cost, probability or loss figure not derived from the supplied facts."],"offline_reachability_review":"A reference memorandum can be created and rendered offline with standard DOCX libraries and office software. Every numeric check follows directly from the request, while the unprovided substantive expectations are standard commercial real estate decision-memo and LOI-risk practices. The four-page cap can accommodate a concise recommendation, comparison, trade-off analysis, authority request and conditional diligence path."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"site_decision_memo","filename":"dunmarrow_ohio_site_decision_memo.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Executive site-selection decision memorandum recommending one Ohio depot property and defining the requested LOI authority.","required":true,"constraints":["The document must be a readable DOCX no longer than four pages, compare August with September, make exactly one site recommendation, and use only supplied or transparently derived figures."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"real_estate_brokers","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"A commercial real estate broker or corporate occupier representative should review the rendered memorandum for a single defensible recommendation, accurate period comparison, treatment of landlord-credit and expansion-right risks, appropriate LOI guardrails, and a workable conditional path. Either Flint under an opening-certainty frame or Alloy under a capacity-preservation frame may pass if the chosen frame, trade-off and conditions are coherent; Canal should not pass as the recommendation because it is undersized for the stated range, below the clearance of the leading sites, unable to meet future dock needs and materially worsened in September.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No external market, legal, engineering, environmental or financial evidence is supplied, so the gold must not resolve those diligence questions or require jurisdiction-specific lease language. Visual page count may vary slightly by renderer; use a standard office rendering and inspect whether the document was intentionally designed within four pages."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:17:58+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:17:58+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:17:58+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:17:58+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R28', 'R29', 'R52', 'P02']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:17:58+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/d902609b81a62396","declared_deliverables":["dunmarrow_ohio_site_decision_memo.docx"]};
